  "coding_notes": [
    "CROSSOVER BLOCK CONFIRMED: 2F q17-q28 = 2H q1-q12, twelve questions worth 40 marks. Predicted from the matching mark sequence, confirmed by reading. Coded in the same sitting as IGCSE-JUN24-F-P2; shared rows carry identical tags by construction.",
    "GAP-CANDIDATE counting_elements_in_sets — q16(c) and q16(d), TWO parts, 2 marks, both asking for n() of a set expression: n(P intersect K complement), and n([P union E] intersect K). Tagged venn_diagrams as an INTERIM measure. This takes the candidate to FOUR parts on the Higher slice, which is the minParts bar. Note how the question separates the two skills cleanly: (a) completing the Venn is venn_diagrams, (b) is conditional probability, and only (c) and (d) are cardinality — the same three-way split seen on Jun25 2H q20, which is what makes the membership/cardinality line operable rather than theoretical.",
    "q25 tagged trig_graphs: reading the maximum and an intercept off a sketched transformed sine curve. graph_transformations was considered but the marks are for reading coordinates off the given sketch, not for describing the transformation.",
    "q13(c) tagged interquartile_range alongside cumulative_frequency — the IQR is the thing being estimated, the graph is how.",
    "No arithmetic series and no calculus on this paper; both of this series' sightings of each were on Paper 1."
  ],
